{'symbol': 'ANSS', 'date': '2022-04-28 09:00:00', 'title': 'ANSYS SUPPORTS HIGH-SPEED DIGITAL ENGINEERING THROUGH NEW GRADUATE PROGRAM', 'text': "THE UNIVERSITY OF COLORADO BOULDER WILL LAUNCH A MASTER'S DEGREE PROGRAM THAT WILL INTEGRATE AND FEATURE ANSYS' BEST-IN-CLASS ELECTRONICS SIMULATION / KEY HIGHLIGHTS ANSYS AND CU BOULDER WILL EQUIP THE NEXT GENERATION OF ELECTRONICS ENGINEERS WITH SIMULATION EXPERIENCE AND SKILL SETS CU BOULDER'S LATEST GRADUATE PROGRAM WILL INCORPORATE ANSYS' LEADING ELECTRONICS SIMULATION SOLUTIONS THROUGH THE ANSYS ELECTRONICS DESKTOP STUDENT DOWNLOAD, WHICH INCLUDES FOUR TOP-TIER SIMULATION APPLICATIONS INDUSTRY INSIGHT FROM ANSYS WILL STRENGTHEN THE ACADEMIC CURRICULUM, BETTER PREPARING STUDENTS FOR CAREERS IN ENGINEERING PITTSBURGH, PA. , APRIL 28, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- IN LINE WITH ITS MISSION TO SUPPORT ENGINEERS AT EVERY STAGE OF THEIR CAREERS, ANSYS\xa0(NASDAQ: ANSS) WILL HELP FACILITATE SIMULATION INTEGRATION AT CU BOULDER THROUGH THE UNIVERSITY'S NEW PROFESSIONAL MASTER'S PROGRAM IN HIGH-SPEED DIGITAL ENGINEERING (PMP-HSDE)."}